# MYTHOS GitHub control bridge — polling timer for the Type=oneshot service.
#
# Schedule design (gh-issue-134, 2026-09-03):
#   OnBootSec=1min          first tick after boot; also fires immediately on any
#                           later timer (re)start because the mark is in the past
#   OnUnitInactiveSec=1min  re-arm 1 min after each oneshot tick FINISHES, so the
#                           chain never overlaps and never depends on ActiveEnter
#   AccuracySec=15s         keep the cadence close to 1 minute
#
# Persistent= is deliberately NOT set. It only has meaning for OnCalendar=, but it
# still makes systemd load the last-trigger stamp on start; with the stamp present
# the already-elapsed OnBootSec mark is disabled as "one-time, fired" and the
# unit-relative base does not exist yet in a fresh user manager, so the timer sits
# at SubState=elapsed / NextElapse=infinity and the bridge stops polling. That is
# exactly what happened after user@1001 restarted on 2026-09-03 16:52:59 UTC.
# Test: tests/mythos-github-bridge-timer-test.js
[Unit]
Description=MYTHOS GitHub control bridge — poll the control branch every 1 minute

[Timer]
OnBootSec=1min
OnUnitInactiveSec=1min
AccuracySec=15s

[Install]
WantedBy=timers.target
